                <pb facs="0923" n="914" xml:id="pg914"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.3331/192</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the Chief of the
                        Division of the American Republics</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Duggan</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-07-07">July 7, 1938</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Uruguayan Minister telephoned me at one o’clock today to state that he had
                    not yet received any word from his Government with regard to the trade agreement
                    proposal. The Minister stated that he had made it clear beyond doubt that a
                    reply would have to be forthcoming by today, so that he felt confident that he
                    would receive a message sometime during the remainder of the day.</p>
                <p>I told the Minister not to hesitate to get in touch with me regardless of the
                    time he received the message.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Laurence Duggan</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
